Texto para Analisar:

The table presents the percentage of people's income spent on different items in five european countries in 2002.
	In general, expenditure on food/drink/tobacco was the most signifcant across all five countries; in addition Italy and Turkey, stood out at clothing/footwear and leisure/education, respectively.
	In terms of food/drink/tobacco expenditure, europeans wasted the highest proportion of their income in this category, with the largest allocation been from Turkey, of 32.14%; even in Italy, which had the lowest rate among them all, they still got 16.36% of their earnings spent in this category.
	Meanwhile, clothing/footwear and leisure/education costs were comparatively lower for all of them. The italians were prominent in the matter of clothing/footwear with exactly 9% and Turkey recorded the highest figures at leisure/education with 4.35%, more than double of the 1.98% of Spain.

R:
**Análise Crítica:**
O texto demonstra boa organização e vocabulário apropriado para uma descrição de gráfico no estilo acadêmico (como IELTS Writing Task 1). No entanto, há alguns problemas de gramática, escolha lexical, capitalização e naturalidade que afetam a fluidez e a precisão. Algumas expressões soam pouco naturais para o inglês acadêmico formal.

---

**Correções:**

* `"five european countries"` → `"five European countries"`
  (Nomes de nacionalidades e continentes devem começar com letra maiúscula.)

* `"most signifcant"` → `"most significant"`
  (Erro ortográfico.)

* `"in addition Italy and Turkey, stood out"` → `"in addition, Italy and Turkey stood out"`
  (Uso incorreto da vírgula.)

* `"stood out at clothing/footwear"` → `"stood out in terms of clothing/footwear"`
  (Preposição inadequada.)

* `"europeans wasted the highest proportion"` → `"Europeans spent the highest proportion"`
  (“Wasted” possui conotação negativa e inadequada para análise de dados.)

* `"with the largest allocation been from Turkey"` → `"with the largest allocation being from Turkey"`
  (Erro gramatical com gerúndio.)

* `"they still got 16.36% of their earnings spent"` → `"people still spent 16.36% of their earnings"`
  (“Got” é informal e a estrutura original soa artificial.)

* `"The italians"` → `"The Italians"`
  (Nacionalidades devem ser capitalizadas.)

* `"were prominent in the matter of clothing/footwear"` → `"spent the highest proportion on clothing/footwear"`
  (Expressão mais natural e objetiva.)

* `"recorded the highest figures at leisure/education"` → `"recorded the highest figures for leisure/education"`
  (Preposição incorreta.)

* `"more than double of the 1.98% of Spain"` → `"more than double Spain's 1.98%"`
  (Estrutura comparativa mais natural.)

---

**Sugestões de Melhoria:**

* Frase original:
  `"The table presents the percentage of people's income spent on different items in five european countries in 2002."`

  Sugestão:
  `"The table illustrates the percentage of household income spent on various categories in five European countries in 2002."`

---

* Frase original:
  `"In general, expenditure on food/drink/tobacco was the most signifcant across all five countries; in addition Italy and Turkey, stood out at clothing/footwear and leisure/education, respectively."`

  Sugestão:
  `"Overall, expenditure on food, drinks, and tobacco accounted for the largest proportion of spending in all five countries, while Italy and Turkey recorded the highest figures for clothing/footwear and leisure/education, respectively."`

---

* Frase original:
  `"In terms of food/drink/tobacco expenditure, europeans wasted the highest proportion of their income in this category, with the largest allocation been from Turkey, of 32.14%; even in Italy, which had the lowest rate among them all, they still got 16.36% of their earnings spent in this category."`

  Sugestão:
  `"Regarding food, drinks, and tobacco, this category represented the largest share of expenditure in all countries. Turkey recorded the highest percentage at 32.14%, whereas Italy had the lowest figure at 16.36%."`

---

* Frase original:
  `"Meanwhile, clothing/footwear and leisure/education costs were comparatively lower for all of them. The italians were prominent in the matter of clothing/footwear with exactly 9% and Turkey recorded the highest figures at leisure/education with 4.35%, more than double of the 1.98% of Spain."`

  Sugestão:
  `"Meanwhile, spending on clothing/footwear and leisure/education was considerably lower across the five countries. Italy allocated the highest proportion to clothing/footwear at exactly 9%, while Turkey spent the most on leisure/education at 4.35%, which was more than double Spain's figure of 1.98%."`

---

**Versão Revisada Completa:**

> "The table illustrates the percentage of household income spent on various categories in five European countries in 2002.
>
> Overall, expenditure on food, drinks, and tobacco accounted for the largest proportion of spending in all five countries, while Italy and Turkey recorded the highest figures for clothing/footwear and leisure/education, respectively.
>
> Regarding food, drinks, and tobacco, this category represented the largest share of expenditure in all countries. Turkey recorded the highest percentage at 32.14%, whereas Italy had the lowest figure at 16.36%.
>
> Meanwhile, spending on clothing/footwear and leisure/education was considerably lower across the five countries. Italy allocated the highest proportion to clothing/footwear at exactly 9%, while Turkey spent the most on leisure/education at 4.35%, which was more than double Spain's figure of 1.98%."




